===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*īwaz}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*h₁eyH-weh₂-}}, a suffixed form of the base {{m|ine-pro|*h₁eyH-||reddish, colourful}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|goh|īwa}} ({{cog|de|Eibe}}), {{cog|gml|īwe}}, {{cog|nl|ijf}}, {{cog|non|ýr||bow, yew}}. The Indo-European root is perhaps also the source of {{cog|sga|ibar}} ({{cog|ga|iúr}}), {{cog|ine-bsl-pro|*eiwas}} ({{cog|lt|ievà}}), {{cog|sla-pro|*jьva}} ({{cog|ru|и́ва||willow}}), {{cog|la|ūva||bunch of grapes}}).

The West Germanic languages have a variant {{m|gem-pro|*īhwaz}} with a guttural consonant, represented by {{cog|ang|ēoh}}.

